    "Exceptional weather": "Vreme excepțională",
    "Simulation is active. ThermalPilot does not control heating.": "Simulare activă. ThermalPilot nu controlează încălzirea.",
    "Observation and learning only; no thermostat control.": "Doar observare și învățare; fără control.",
    "ThermalPilot controls thermostat targets.": "ThermalPilot controlează țintele termostatelor.",
    "Seasonal fallback temperatures are used.": "Se folosesc temperaturi sezoniere de rezervă.",
    "Scheduled targets remain simulated; season transitions can change thermostat targets.": "Plan simulat; schimbările sezoniere pot modifica ținte reale.",
    "Live thermostat control is not enabled.": "Control real neactivat.",
    "Target changes include the shared start/stop offsets. The temperature forecast models the planned heating period; actual valve and heat-pump delays must be checked against observations.": "Include decalaje de început/final. Verificați întârzieri reale ale valvelor și pompei.",
    "These forecasts were saved 1, 3 or 6 hours before the measurements. Later readings do not change them. Lower error is better; compare it with simply predicting no temperature change. Different heating, computers and other heat sources can affect the result.": "Prognoze salvate cu 1, 3 sau 6 ore înainte, apoi neschimbate. Abatere mică mai bună; comparați cu temperatură constantă. Alte surse afectează rezultatul.",
    "Compare recorded temperatures with forecasts saved hours earlier. The accuracy cards also compare against predicting no temperature change. Forecasts assume the proposed heating plan; actual heating may differ, especially during simulation.": "Comparați cu prognoze vechi și temperatură constantă. Încălzirea reală poate diferi, mai ales în simulare.",
    "Forecasts are compared with measurements within five minutes of their due time. “Similar heating” means observed demand matched the forecast for at least 90% of observations, with no large recording gaps. These counts give context, not a guarantee of accuracy.": "Măsurare în cinci minute. Încălzire similară: ≥90% potrivire fără goluri mari. Numerele nu garantează precizie.",
    "Each row shows the latest observation within its 15-minute interval, not an average. Suggested thermostat target is the setting ThermalPilot would apply, not a room-temperature forecast. Table shows up to 288 intervals. Original observations remain stored internally. Short chart views use 15-minute time labels; longer views use wider intervals.": "Ultima observație pe 15 minute, nu medie. Ținta este setare, nu prognoză. Până la 288 intervale; originale păstrate.",
    "Suggested On means the boosted target window, including valve timing offsets. Relay On means observed demand; it does not guarantee heat flow.": "Pornit sugerat este țintă crescută cu decalaje. Releu pornit arată cerere, nu căldură garantată.",
    ", without heating, remaining slab warmth or appliance heat. Lower temperature loss means slower modeled cooling. This is a model estimate, not measured energy efficiency or an insulation rating.": ", fără încălzire, căldură reziduală sau aparate. Pierdere mică înseamnă răcire lentă modelată, nu eficiență sau izolație.",
    "Cooling-speed bands are provisional: under 1 h, 1–2 h, 2–4 h, 4–8 h, and 8 h or longer per 1°C drop. For a selected house type, badges instead compare with that type: under 0.5×, 0.5–0.8×, 0.8–1.25×, 1.25–2×, and at least 2× its reference cooling time. Initial rooms share starting estimates and remain unrated. Comparisons become more useful as their heat-loss parameters adapt to observations. Wind, ventilation, sensor placement and unmeasured heat sources can affect the estimates. The listed time describes this reference test, not how long heating can safely remain off in your home.": "Modele inițiale egale. Vânt, ventilație, senzori și alte surse influențează comparația. Timpul de referință nu este durată sigură fără încălzire.",
    "Learned parameters and season aggregates are retained when old observations are compacted.": "Parametrii învățați și totalurile sezoniere rămân la compactare.",
    "Open a Home Assistant dashboard once, then return here to load embedded history cards.": "Deschideți un panou Home Assistant, apoi reveniți pentru istoric.",
    "Water-based systems only: raise the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session, allowing slow valves to open. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no advance offset.": "Doar apă: creștere anticipată pentru valve lente. Electric/aer ignoră decalajul.",
    "Water-based systems only: lower the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session ends, allowing valves to close. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no closing offset.": "Doar apă: reducere înainte de final pentru valve. Electric/aer ignoră decalajul.",
    "What produces heat for your house. Select air-to-water for your water floor system supplied by an air-source heat pump. Gas, oil, wood and district heating need their own fuel-cost logic; choosing a house detail does not yet enable a different controller or reset learned room data.": "Sursa casei. Combustibilii nu primesc control de cost propriu; datele rămân.",
    "How heat reaches rooms: circulating water in floors or radiators, electric floor/ceiling/panels, or warm air. Mixed means different rooms use different systems. Water distribution can optionally use a heating-water sensor and uses valve timing. Electric and warm-air distribution ignore those inputs and learn response from observed thermostat demand. Mixed and Other retain water requirements until room overrides are supported.": "Apa folosește timpi valve și senzor opțional. Electric/aer învață din cerere. Mixt păstrează setări apă.",
    "The construction around floor heating, which affects how slowly heat is stored and released. Concrete slab describes your heated floor. Choose Not applicable if there is no floor heating. This does not change your configured response lag or erase learned parameters.": "Podeaua influențează stocarea. Fără încălzire în pardoseală: Nu se aplică. Nu schimbă întârzierea sau modelul.",
    "The structure below your home: slab on ground, crawl space or basement. A heated concrete floor can be above a basement, so this is separate from Heated floor. Choose Unknown if unsure. This descriptive setting does not reset observation history or learned models.": "Fundație separată de podea. Alege Necunoscut dacă nesigur. Modele și istoric rămân.",
    "Sunlight through large windows, especially south-facing windows, can warm a room. No additional physical solar heating system is needed. Select the main direction of those windows to enable solar estimates, or Solar heating off to turn them off. Home Assistant’s location determines seasonal sun elevation and azimuth; cloud conditions come from your weather source. The effect starts at zero and learns gradually. Missing sunlight data assumes no solar warmth; room temperature limits still apply.": "Soare prin ferestre mari, fără sistem solar. Direcție, locație și nori dau aport, învățat de la zero. Fără date: fără aport; limitele rămân.",
    "Clear means the windows receive direct sunlight without major obstructions. Choose Partly shaded for some trees, buildings or overhangs, or Mostly shaded when sunlight is usually blocked. Forecasts use a more cautious solar allowance: partly shaded uses 65% and mostly shaded 30% of the clear allowance. Actual room warming is still learned from observations; no solar heat is assumed before learning. Seasonal leaf cover and changing shading can still affect accuracy.": "Liber, parțial sau mult umbrit: 100%, 65% sau 30% aport solar. Căldura reală învățată; umbra poate varia.",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Vânt opțional, unități automate, medie 30 min. Efect învățat din date variate. Lipsă, invalid sau constant 2 ore ignorat; încălzirea continuă. Prognoza îndepărtată revine la vânt tipic.",
    "Emergency lower temperature limit shared by all rooms. Each room’s own target is the normal comfort goal. ThermalPilot prioritizes avoiding this limit even when electricity is expensive; this value is not the idle thermostat target.": "Limită absolută, nu țintă de repaus. Ținta camerei este confort; limita protejată în ore scumpe.",
    "Upper temperature limit shared by all rooms. Extra heating and heat storage must stay within this limit.": "Limită maximă comună; căldura suplimentară nu o depășește.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Prognoză relativă opțională după prețuri confirmate. Unități și costuri suplimentare inutile. Poate crește rezerva, niciodată preț confirmat sau comandă viitoare directă. Lipsă: plan normal.",
    "Notify in Home Assistant when a room temperature sensor stays unchanged or unavailable for this many hours. A stable room can also have an unchanged reading, so the warning asks you to check the sensor. ThermalPilot sends at most one sensor notification per calendar day. Monitoring runs while ThermalPilot is active; long monitoring gaps restart the timer.": "Avertizează după acest timp fără citire nouă.",
    "Summer fallback always applies from 15.5. through 30.9. Outside those dates, it also applies when the day’s lowest forecast temperature is equal to or above this value. For example, a setting of 6°C means the daily minimum must be at least 6°C for ThermalPilot to use summer fallback temperatures. Lower readings already observed that day are included. If a full-day forecast is unavailable outside the summer dates, winter fallback is used.": "Rezervă vară 15.5.–30.9., altfel dacă minimul întregii zile atinge limita. Lipsa prognozei nu activează vara în afara datelor.",
    "Negative values reduce estimated heat loss while the fireplace is active; −20% means a 20% reduction.": "Negativ reduce pierderea cu șemineu activ; −20% înseamnă 20% mai puțin.",
    "Prefer a sensor that includes electricity prices and additional costs, such as VAT, transfer tariffs, electricity tax and retailer margin. A variable electricity-price sensor without these costs also works. If transfer tariffs differ between day and night, including them helps ThermalPilot choose the cheapest heating hours; omitting them can shift heating to hours that are less economical overall. Select a source containing today/tomorrow or timestamped raw_today/raw_tomorrow price lists, and choose the matching source price unit.": "Preferabil preț total cu taxe, rețea și marjă. Prețul variabil singur funcționează; lipsa tarifelor rețelei zi/noapte poate afecta orele. Folosiți today/tomorrow sau raw_today/raw_tomorrow datate și unitate corectă.",
    "Hourly average uses fixed hourly averages of the source prices. 15 minutes plans using quarter-hour intervals. Flexible builds heating sessions in 15-minute steps, allowing runs such as 60 or 75 minutes while respecting the minimum flexible heating run.": "Medie orară, interval 15 min sau flexibil în pași de 15 min cu minim.",
    "The shortest planned heating session in flexible scheduling mode. Longer sessions can be chosen in 15-minute steps. This setting applies to flexible runs; valve opening and closing offsets are applied separately.": "Sesiune minimă flexibilă; mai lungi în pași 15 min.",
    "Initial estimate of how slowly heat input affects room temperature and how long its effect persists. Concrete slabs often need a longer delay, but lightweight floors, radiators, electric heaters and air systems also have a response time. Use a shorter value for faster systems. This remains relevant to every distribution; it is separate from valve opening or closing time.": "Estimare inițială de inerție și efect rezidual; modelul învață.",
    "The warm outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or warmer, the starting model assumes the lower daily heating need. This curve seeds the model before enough real heating and cooling observations are available.": "Punct cald al necesarului zilnic inițial; răspuns real învățat.",
    "The cold outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or colder, the starting model assumes the higher daily heating need. Set it below the warm endpoint. Actual room response is learned from observations.": "Punct rece inițial sub cel cald; răspuns real învățat.",
    "Allows real thermostat setpoint changes when ThermalPilot changes between Active and Passive. Active applies each room’s target temperature; Passive applies the seasonal fallback: the shared summer setpoint or each room’s normal target in winter. These commands can occur even with simulation enabled. This does not enable live heating schedule control.": "Schimbări sezoniere reale și în simulare. Activ: ținta camerei; pasiv: rezervă vară/iarnă. Fără control program.",
    "The thermostat target used for all configured rooms while ThermalPilot is Passive, if real Active/Passive season setpoint control is enabled. A low summer target normally prevents heating without switching off the thermostats.": "Țintă comună vară în pasiv cu control sezonier. Ținta mică evită încălzirea fără oprirea termostatelor.",
    "Degrees added to each room’s target temperature during a suggested heating window. For example, a 20 °C target with a 1.5 °C boost suggests a 21.5 °C thermostat setpoint to store heat. Scheduled targets remain simulated in this version.": "Grade peste țintă pentru stocare, ex. 20 + 1,5 = 21,5°C.",
    "Negative values temporarily lower the thermostat target during expensive electricity hours. After a planned heating session, ThermalPilot first restores the room’s normal target. It then chooses reduction only when predicted stored warmth can avoid thermostat heating while supporting room comfort. For example, −1°C allows a 20°C target to be reduced to 19°C during selected costly hours. The reduced target never goes below Minimum allowed temperature. Normal target is restored when reduction is no longer useful; a new planned heating session uses the boosted target. Duration is chosen by the plan, not a fixed number of hours.": "Reducere negativă în ore scumpe cu rezervă suficientă. Mai întâi normal după sesiune, niciodată sub minim. Restabilește când inutil; durata din plan.",
    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Temperatură măsurată opțională; climate folosește current_temperature, nu țintă. Corectează puterea. Lipsa nu oprește învățare/plan și nu forțează rezerva.",
    "Simulation calculates heating suggestions without applying scheduled targets. Disable simulation and confirm to enable real thermostat control. If another automation controls these thermostats, disable it first. Observation and learning continue in both modes.": "Simularea nu aplică ținte. Opriți și confirmați pentru control real; opriți altă automatizare dacă există. Învățare în ambele moduri.",
    "Choose the interface language. Room and entity names remain unchanged. Save settings to keep the choice. Embedded history cards follow this choice where supported by Home Assistant.": "Alege limba și salvează. Numele rămân. Istoricul integrat urmează unde este suportat.",
    "All room timelines share the price chart’s time axis.${zones.length?' Zone rows show recorded heating and cooling only; off and standby periods stay empty. Plan adds suggested heating only for tariff-optimized zones.':''} Teal shows the suggested thermostat boost window; amber shows observed heating demand. ": "Axă comună. Turcoaz: creștere; portocaliu: cerere observată. ",
    "The selected period controls past history. Today and tomorrow are included when prices are published. Recorded activity is shown before now; future suggestions follow the current plan. Price gaps stay empty. ": "Perioada definește istoric; azi/mâine cu prețuri. Înainte observații; după plan actual. Goluri preț goale. ",
    "Times align to 15-minute boundaries; wider views show fewer labels. Hover, focus or tap a price bar or heating period for details.": "Limite 15 min; vederi lungi mai puține etichete. Indicați, focalizați sau atingeți pentru detalii.",
    "This measures initial data collection, not model trustworthiness. Continue validating forecasts and heating suggestions before enabling live control. Learning continues after initial data collection.": "Colectarea inițială nu este fiabilitate. Validați înainte de control; învățarea continuă.",
    "History collection and learning paused because outdoor temperature is unavailable. Existing model parameters are retained.": "Istoric și învățare în pauză fără temperatură exterioară. Modelul rămâne.",
    "No weather forecast: current outdoor temperature is held constant.": "Fără prognoză meteo; exteriorul considerat constant.",
    "Live control awaits confirmation. Enable simulation, save, then disable it and confirm to activate thermostat control.": "Controlul așteaptă confirmare. Simulare pornită, salvare, apoi oprită și confirmare.",
    "Waiting for enough heating and idle observations to estimate the remaining time.": "Se așteaptă mai multe observații pentru estimarea timpului.",
    "A door/window contact sensor can monitor the fireplace damper position. Select the sensor state that means the fireplace is in use. For a damper contact sensor, Open normally means active and Closed means inactive. Door/window labels are converted to Home Assistant’s underlying on/off values. Other sensors show their declared options, current valid state and any saved value. A contact state indicates the damper position; it does not prove that a fire is burning.": "Contact ușă/geam pe clapetă: Deschis de obicei activ, Închis inactiv. Salvat on/off. Alte senzori arată opțiuni. Poziția nu dovedește foc aprins.",
    "Measured temperature (°C)": "Temperatură măsurată (°C)",
    "Suggested thermostat target (°C)": "Țintă sugerată termostat (°C)",
